docs: the cache setting is "defer to this file", not "bypass"

Cache Rules name three Edge TTL choices; the one this site wants is "Use cache control-header if present, bypass cache if not", which makes the committed `_headers` the cache policy. A blanket Bypass works and is worse — it discards any future ability to cache from a file in git. And strictly no rule is needed: Cloudflare does not cache HTML or JSON by default and Origin Cache Control is on by default, so the platform already respects the file; its fallback TTLs apply only when no cache headers are present.

Corrects the "Edge TTL = Bypass" recommendation in both `_headers` and OPEN.md §2b, which was imprecise advice sitting in a merged file.
